body:
DEC03 rev 3 is ready under tests/hw/vdec/ (N2TEST DEC03 PASS 2781/2781). The hook signature is unchanged from my 17:31 post; the integration needs four call sites in n2vc_hw_fake.c, and the POLL loop is the important one (otherwise the vendor's VLD 0xe8 / AVC 0x2d8 polls never see the model).

Proposed API in tests/hw/n2vc_hw_fake.h:

  typedef int (*n2vc_hw_fake_reg_hook)(void *ctx, unsigned win, uint32_t off,
                                       int is_write, uint32_t *value);
  int n2vc_hw_fake_set_reg_hook(struct n2vc_hw *hw, n2vc_hw_fake_reg_hook fn, void *ctx);

Semantics: return 1 = handled (*value is the read result / the write was stored by the hook), 0 = use the fake's normal array/rules, <0 = error. Call it only after check_reg() and the block_on() power check.

1) In fake_regs(), READ case, before find_read_rule/read_word:
     if (f->hook) { uint32_t hv = 0; int hr = f->hook(f->hook_ctx, o->window, o->offset, 0, &hv);
                    if (hr < 0) { rc = hr; break; }
                    if (hr > 0) { v = hv; write_record_as_usual; break; } }
2) WRITE case before write_word: same with is_write=1; if hr > 0, skip write_word/apply_rules.
3) WRITE_MASK: compute the merged value through the hook's own shadow:
     old = read_word(...); if (f->hook) { hv=old; hr=hook(...,0,&hv); if (hr>0) old=hv; }
     v = (old & ~o->mask) | (o->value & o->mask);
     if (f->hook) { hv=v; hr=hook(...,1,&hv); if (hr>0) v=hv; }
     write_word(...,v); apply_rules(... v & mask ...)
   (The vendor uses masked writes on AVC 0x2c8, VLD 0xec/0x140 and the larb; without this the model's stored value can diverge.)
4) POLL: inside the per-read loop, ask the hook for a read before read_word/find_read_rule; use hv when hr>0. Then the normal mask/timeout check.

Window 12: the model maps RWVC_WIN_VDEC_ALL as base 0x16000000 size 0x30000. The fake's window table must accept it (DEC07/DEC04 are proposing that entry); until then the model is usable only through wins 4/7/8/9, which cover the VLD/AVC/MISC/LAT pages but not the LAT_AVC 0x12000 page. If you prefer, I can supply a small adapter that wraps an existing struct n2vc_hw (like t_vld.c's bridge) with no change to your file; tell me which you want. No phone, no publish.
